WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 3.2 · Structure, Governance & Accountability
Organisational structures and organigrams

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Draw the structure you start with and the one you expect as you grow, and change it on purpose.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:25.541
An organigram is a simple chart of roles and who reports to whom. It shows how the work is organised, not who approves spending or how decisions are made.

4
00:00:25.941 --> 00:00:26.541
Common shapes to start from

5
00:00:26.541 --> 00:00:38.611
Functional: Roles grouped by expertise, such as delivery, finance and communications. Most new organisations start here. For example: A bakery cooperative: one founder leads baking, the other leads sales and accounts.

6
00:00:38.611 --> 00:00:48.830
Programme or product: Roles grouped around each programme, product or service you offer. For example: A youth club with one lead for sports and another for homework help.

7
00:00:48.830 --> 00:01:00.248
Network or hub: A small core of founders coordinating partners and volunteers around them. For example: Two repair café founders coordinate ten volunteer fixers and a host venue.

8
00:01:00.648 --> 00:01:01.248
Why draw it now

9
00:01:01.248 --> 00:01:06.552
1. Everyone can see who does what and who to ask.

10
00:01:06.552 --> 00:01:12.226
2. You notice when one founder becomes the bottleneck for every decision.

11
00:01:12.226 --> 00:01:18.900
3. Funders and partners see a real, honest picture of your team.

12
00:01:19.300 --> 00:01:19.900
What it guides

13
00:01:19.900 --> 00:01:25.574
1. Your governance, shown apart from management, even with the same founders.

14
00:01:25.574 --> 00:01:31.248
2. Your role cards and delegation of authority, built on these lines.

15
00:01:31.248 --> 00:01:38.663
3. Your growth: the chart for today and for two or three years ahead.

16
00:01:39.063 --> 00:01:39.663
What to avoid

17
00:01:39.663 --> 00:01:43.856
Drawing ten empty boxes to look established.

18
00:01:43.856 --> 00:01:48.789
Mixing governance and management in one set of lines.

19
00:01:48.789 --> 00:01:55.833
Using personal details instead of role names, or changing shape by accident.

20
00:01:56.433 --> 00:01:58.233
You map your starting roles, reporting lines and capacity gaps.

21
00:01:58.233 --> 00:02:02.233
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

22
00:02:03.733 --> 00:02:06.833
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
